# Fix lesson player shared-ref wiring (transcript timestamps)

Found while researching the YouTube-style touch-gesture layer (2026-08-20). Vojta confirmed the bug reproduces. Autoplay/binge is NOT affected (it reads cookie prefs and plays on the local ref, no context needed).

**Status: fix implemented in PR #134 (feat/player-touch-gestures) together with the gesture layer — close this task when that PR merges.**

## Transcript timestamps do nothing on lesson pages

`AuthedVideoPlayer` keeps a local `playerRef` but never publishes it to the shared `MuxPlayerProvider` context — the `setMuxPlayerRef(playerRef)` call at `apps/ai-hero/src/app/(content)/_components/authed-video-player.tsx:199` is commented out. `VideoTranscriptRenderer`'s mm:ss buttons write `muxPlayerRef.current.currentTime` into a null ref, so clicking a transcript timestamp does not seek.

Fix: publish the ref (re-add `setMuxPlayerRef(playerRef)` in `onLoadedData`), then verify transcript seek on a lesson page. `PostPlayer` already does this in an effect (`post-player.tsx:76-78`) — mirror that.

## Ruled out: `playsInline`

The lesson player not passing `playsInline` is a non-issue — verified in `@mux/mux-player@3.13.0/dist/base.mjs`: the internal `<mux-video>` template carries a bare unconditional `playsinline` attribute, so inline playback on iOS is already guaranteed for every Mux player in the app. Do not add the prop.

## Context

Companion fix to the planned YouTube-style gesture layer for the Mux player (learner feedback from Matt's Discord, 2026-08-19: tiny controls on iPad/phone, wants big play/pause + 10s back/forward). Spec: `apps/ai-hero/docs/mux-player-touch-gestures-spec.md`. The gesture layer itself takes the player ref as a direct prop, so it does not depend on this fix.
